# Licensing

This repository is **multi-licensed**. Every source file carries an
`SPDX-License-Identifier` header that is authoritative for that file. The full
license texts live in [`LICENSES/`](LICENSES/).

| Part of the tree | License | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `firmware/m1-hogp/` (the bridge firmware) | `LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause` | Derived from Nordic Semiconductor's `central_hids` nRF Connect SDK sample. |
| `firmware/boards/` (CX-40 board support) | `Apache-2.0` | Backported from upstream Zephyr / nRF Connect SDK board definitions. |
| `firmware/m1-erase/`, `firmware/m1-hogp/pm_static.yml` (original glue) | `Apache-2.0` | Original work by the repository author. |

## Important: the Nordic 5-Clause license restricts the chip

The bridge firmware (`firmware/m1-hogp/`) is governed by
`LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause`. Clause 4 of that license states the software
**"must only be used with a Nordic Semiconductor ASA integrated circuit."**

This is not a problem for this project — it targets the nRF52840, which is a
Nordic SoC. But it does mean you **cannot lift the `m1-hogp` code onto a
non-Nordic chip** (e.g. an ESP32 or RP2040). The `Apache-2.0` parts
(`boards/`, `m1-erase/`) carry no such restriction.

See [`NOTICE`](NOTICE) for attribution details.
